BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 790 Td /F1 15 Tf (Unit 3 - Normalization \(CS301 Database Management Systems\)) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* () Tj T* (Normalization organizes a relational schema to reduce redundancy and avoid) Tj T* (update, insert and delete anomalies. We decompose a relation into smaller) Tj T* (relations using functional dependencies \(FDs\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (A functional dependency X -> Y means that the value of X determines Y.) Tj T* (Example: in Student\(RollNo, Name, Dept, HOD\), RollNo -> Name, Dept and Dept -> HOD.) Tj T* () Tj T* (First Normal Form \(1NF\): every attribute holds a single atomic value.) Tj T* (A column storing a list of phone numbers violates 1NF; move phones to their) Tj T* (own table StudentPhone\(RollNo, Phone\).) Tj T* ET
endstream
