BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 790 Td /F1 15 Tf (Third Normal Form \(3NF\)) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* () Tj T* (A relation is in 3NF if it is in 2NF and no non-key attribute depends on another) Tj T* (non-key attribute \(no transitive dependency\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (Worked example: Student\(RollNo, Name, Dept, HOD\) with RollNo -> Dept and Dept -> HOD.) Tj T* (HOD depends on RollNo only through Dept, a transitive dependency. If a department) Tj T* (changes its HOD we must update many rows \(update anomaly\).) Tj T* (Decompose into Student\(RollNo, Name, Dept\) and Department\(Dept, HOD\).) Tj T* (Both relations are now in 3NF and the join on Dept is lossless.) Tj T* () Tj T* (BCNF is a stricter form: for every FD X -> Y, X must be a superkey.) Tj T* ET
endstream
